+/**
+ * wlan_mgmt_txrx_external_tx() - account a caller-owned management transfer
+ * @peer: real host owner (may differ from the firmware transport endpoint)
+ * @cookie: caller token, checked before accepting a firmware completion
+ * @context: retained until the completion callback finishes
+ * @send: synchronous submission; firmware must echo the caller's wire token
+ * @complete: exactly one terminal callback after ownership was accepted
+ *
+ * No nbuf is mapped, unmapped or freed here. A DRAINED callback only releases
+ * host bookkeeping. The caller retains ambiguous DMA memory until device
+ * quiescence. Submission must be stopped/joined before vdev/pdev drain, as
+ * with the ordinary management TX API. No callback is made if descriptor
+ * reservation fails. Once send is called, even a send failure gets a callback.
+ *
+ * Return: SUCCESS once ownership is accepted (including synchronous send
+ * failure, which is reported by complete); an error means no callback.
+ */
